  "method_notes": [
    "Within-run observations on repeatedly inspected cases; not held out and not a general superiority claim.",
    "Baseline receives original full histories. No-scene retains source passages in search but disables scene opening and neighbor navigation. Full enables search, recent, and scene navigation.",
    "500 grade-accounting records per arm include administrative zeros for reader failures; actual Terra verdict counts exclude these.",
    "Strict original-attempt sensitivity counts cases with interrupted unfinished original attempts as zero; no captured valid answer was regenerated.",
    "Reader wall time includes client startup, excludes ingestion and judging; not directly comparable to the earlier Sol native reader-turn timing. P95 uses linear interpolation at (n-1)*0.95.",
    "Token input includes cached repeated prefixes, system, harness and tool content; it is neither unique corpus read nor actual billing. Reasoning output is a subset of output.",
    "Titan action totals count recorded wrapper actions excluding instructions, as defined by the run\u2019s tool_count function; wrapper_actions separately includes instruction fetches. Native model-issued tool-call totals were not established. Baseline also made two empty catalog probes, neither returned evidence.",
    "No source-credit audit was performed for this comparison. R5 source run: rubric 477/500 and source credit 410/500; legacy R2 card: rubric 477/500 and source credit 408/500.",
    "Wrapper action timers include prompt checks, retrieval or reading, and serialization after the case lock; they exclude startup, transport, model execution and other work. Every logged search, recent and scene action is included, including errors. Baseline has no memory action timer. The action-time to complete client wall-time figure is a ratio of sums, not model generation timing; remaining wall time includes other work. P95 uses linear interpolation at (n-1)*0.95."
  ]
